.TH AGMUX 1 "2026" "agmux 0.6.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
agmux \- a terminal control panel for tmux and AI coding agents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agmux
[\fI\,--no-preview\/\fR] [\fI\,--no-notify\/\fR] [\fI\,--no-resources\/\fR] [\fI\,command\/\fR] [\fI\,args\/\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B agmux
lists and manages tmux sessions that run AI coding agents such as Codex,
OpenCode, or Claude Code, and plain shells. It is a single, dependency\-free
Python file that reads local tmux metadata and makes no network requests.
.PP
Each session line shows
.B cpu X%
and
.B mem Y
for that session: the machine CPU and RAM used by its processes. These are not
token, context\-window, or rate\-limit figures; those appear in the usage panel
(Rate limits and session cost are read locally).
.PP
Run with no command to open the picker. Type to filter, use Up/Down to select,
and press Enter to attach (or switch your current tmux client).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list, ls
One line per session with agent, state, directory, and CPU/memory. Add
.B --json
for machine\-readable output, or
.B --no-resources
to skip the CPU/memory sample.
.TP
.B info SESSION
Show one session's agent, state, directory, panes, attached clients, and
CPU/memory. Add
.B --json
for machine\-readable output.
.TP
.B attach SESSION
Attach outside tmux; switch the current client inside tmux.
.TP
.B new NAME
Start an agent or shell in a named session. Options:
.BR --agent ,
.BR --cwd ,
.BR --shell ,
.BR --detach ,
.BR --no-notify .
Arguments after
.B --
are passed to the agent.
.TP
.B rename SESSION NAME
Rename a session.
.TP
.B shell SESSION
Add a detached shell window in the session's directory.
.TP
.B delete SESSION
End a session after typing its exact name. Alias:
.BR kill .
.B --yes
skips the typed confirmation for that one session.
.TP
.B usage
Show locally available provider usage (Codex rate limits, OpenCode session cost).
Add
.B --json
for machine\-readable output.
.TP
.B agents
List known agents and whether their binaries are installed.
.TP
.B preview SESSION
Print recent output from the active pane.
.TP
.B peek SESSION
Read\-only live viewer that never attaches a client or forwards input.
.TP
.B watch
Notify when any agent starts waiting for input. Options:
.BR --interval ,
.BR --once ,
.BR --no-notify .
.TP
.B last
Switch back to the previous session (inside tmux).
.TP
.B detach
Detach the current tmux client.
.TP
.B doctor
Report tools, paths, config, and integration status.
.SH KEY BINDINGS (picker)
Type to filter; Up/Down or Tab to select; Enter to attach; Ctrl\-N new session;
Ctrl\-G usage panel; Ctrl\-R rename; Ctrl\-D delete; Ctrl\-W add shell window;
Ctrl\-O read\-only viewer; Ctrl\-P toggle preview; Ctrl\-L refresh; Ctrl\-U clear
search; F1 help; Esc cancel.
.PP
Inside tmux, Ctrl\-b then Ctrl\-s opens the picker in a popup. The shipped
.B tmux.conf
also binds Alt\-s to detach the current client and run the picker directly in
the same terminal, and Alt\-x to kill the current session after a y/n
confirmation. Alt\-x stops every program in that session; the picker's Ctrl\-D
flow is the safer, typed\-name alternative.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Environment variables override the optional config file
.B ~/.config/agmux/config
(override its location with
.BR AGMUX_CONFIG ).
The file uses simple
.I key = value
lines; recognized keys are
.BR repos ,
.BR agent ,
.BR tmux_socket ,
.BR notify ,
.BR notify_cmd ,
.BR watch_interval ,
.BR blocked_patterns ,
.BR working_patterns ,
.BR trim_chrome ,
.BR resources ,
.BR ascii ,
.BR bin ,
.BR codex_home ,
and
.BR opencode_data_dir .
.PP
.B AGMUX_REPOS
lists the project roots shown by the new\-session wizard; separate several
directories with
.BR : .
Defaults to
.BR ~/source/repos .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/agmux/config
optional settings file
.TP
.I ~/.local/bin/agmux
installed command
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.BR AGMUX_AGENT ,
.BR AGMUX_REPOS ,
.BR AGMUX_TMUX_SOCKET ,
.BR AGMUX_NOTIFY ,
.BR AGMUX_NOTIFY_CMD ,
.BR AGMUX_WATCH_INTERVAL ,
.BR AGMUX_BLOCKED_PATTERNS ,
.BR AGMUX_WORKING_PATTERNS ,
.BR AGMUX_TRIM_CHROME ,
.BR AGMUX_RESOURCES ,
.BR AGMUX_ASCII ,
.BR AGMUX_BIN ,
.BR AGMUX_CONFIG ,
.BR CODEX_HOME ,
.BR OPENCODE_DATA_DIR .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tmux (1)
